total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Bounty:** $25 (LT)\n\nREPO: https://github.com/lobster-trap/TentOfTrials\n\nCreate a `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root. This is the instruction file Claude Code reads on startup to understand the project. Right now it has to figure everything out by reading 50K of README.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Create `CLAUDE.md` (max 500 lines) covering: project purpose, tech stack per directory, common dev commands, coding conventions, and known pitfalls\n- Must include the build-and-diagnostic workflow: \"Always run `python3 build.py` after changes and include the diagnostic artifacts in your PR\"\n- Include a \"Where to start\" section for each module (which file to read first)\n- The tone should match the repo's existing self-deprecating style (read README.md and a few source files for reference)\n- No markdown lint errors (run through a linter or validate manually)\n\nRequired validation:\n- Run `python3 build.py`\n- Include the generated diagnostic `.logd` artifact from `diagnostic/build-XXX.logd` in the PR notes; also include `diagnostic/build-XXX.json` if present\n- You must use `.github/pull_request_template.md` for your submission","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4","id":4148310747,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjLb","number":4,"title":"[BOUNTY $150] AGENT: Claude Code sub-agent that reviews a PR and posts a structured comment","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402697,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e2CQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/agent","name":"agent","color":"059669","default":false,"description":"Claude Code agent"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1065,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:18:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $150 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate a Claude Code agent that takes a PR diff as input, analyzes it,\nand returns a structured Markdown review comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Works via CLI: `claude-review --pr https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/123`\n- [ ] OR via GitHub Action (include the workflow YAML)\n- [ ] Structured Markdown output with:\n  - Summary of changes (2–3 sentences)\n  - Identified risks (list)\n  - Improvement suggestions (list)\n  - Confidence score: Low / Medium / High\n- [ ] Tested on at least 2 real GitHub PRs (include outputs in the PR)\n- [ ] README with setup and usage instructions\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with the agent + sample outputs\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/issues/1638","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/issues/1638/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/issues/1638/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/issues/1638/events","html_url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-llk/issues/1638","id":4393226410,"node_id":"I_kwDONp7J8c8AAAABBdtQqg","number":1638,"title":"[Bounty $1000] Reduce RISCV instructions used to pass on tensix instructions using AI/Optimizer.","user":{"login":"amahmudTT","id":173845504,"node_id":"U_kgDOClysAA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173845504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT","html_url":"https://github.com/amahmudTT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amahmudTT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8181863245,"node_id":"LA_kwDONp7J8c8AAAAB561TTQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/labels/P2","name":"P2","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null},{"id":8201774933,"node_id":"LA_kwDONp7J8c8AAAAB6N0nVQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null},{"id":8201775094,"node_id":"LA_kwDONp7J8c8AAAAB6N0n9g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/labels/bounty_difficulty/medium","name":"bounty_difficulty/medium","color":"EE8199","default":false,"description":null},{"id":8569560458,"node_id":"LA_kwDONp7J8c8AAAAB_skdig","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/labels/LLK","name":"LLK","color":"FECA4C","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"Zaneham","id":222171382,"node_id":"U_kgDODT4Q9g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/222171382?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham","html_url":"https://github.com/Zaneham","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":22,"created_at":"2026-05-06T17:27:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:30:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"Zaneham","id":222171382,"node_id":"U_kgDODT4Q9g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/222171382?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham","html_url":"https://github.com/Zaneham","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zaneham/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The number of tensix instructions to do a particular task can be easily optimized with human thinking, as the main task would have an algorithm and the proper instructions and sequence can often be easily chosen. But to pass on the tensix insturctions to the tensix engine, we often use MOPs and Replay buffers to pass them so that the number of RISCV instructions are rerduced. That part has too many ways of accomplishing and is not too easy to find out what is the most optimal way all the time. \n\nThis is where we can use AI to reduce the number of RISV instructions used, by varying the possibilities of writing the MOP and arrangement of the replay buffer. Overall the task is \n\nObjective : Minimize the number of RISCV instructions to issue instructions to tensix engine \nConstraints : Sequence of tensix instructions passed remains the same\n                       Only specified amount of replay buffer is used (for example if Math thread uses whole of the buffer, it may clash with SFPU algorithms when they are run from a separate thread on WH/BH for the buffer being shared. \n                        Take into account two ways of writing mops and their constraints. \n\nAn AI agent may be asked to do it for all the ops we have and then we filter out the good suggestions and apply them. ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/issues/1638/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-llk/issues/1638/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/32187","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/32187/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/32187/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/32187/events","html_url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/32187","id":3609136414,"node_id":"I_kwDOI9Wqc87XHw0e","number":32187,"title":"[Bounty $1500] LLVC (Low-Latency Low-Resource Voice Conversion) bring up using TTNN APIs","user":{"login":"tvardhineniTT","id":225911693,"node_id":"U_kgDODXcjjQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225911693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT","html_url":"https://github.com/tvardhineniTT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvardhineniTT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7931645110,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI9Wqc88AAAAB2MNMtg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null},{"id":7931705304,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI9Wqc88AAAAB2MQ32A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/labels/bounty_difficulty/medium","name":"bounty_difficulty/medium","color":"EE8199","default":false,"description":"Medium Bounty"},{"id":9462912915,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI9Wqc88AAAACNAiXkw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/labels/model%20bringup","name":"model bringup","color":"fa8c2b","default":false,"description":"For model initialization or bring-up stage bounties"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":52,"created_at":"2025-11-10T18:07:10Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:25:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### 📝 Background\n\nThis bounty is for bringing up the **LLVC (Low-Latency Low-Resource Voice Conversion)** model using TTNN APIs on Tenstorrent hardware (Wormhole or Blackhole).\n\nLLVC is a real-time voice conversion model from Koe AI specifically optimized for low latency and CPU efficiency. Published in 2023, key features include:\n\n* **Ultra-low latency**: Designed for real-time voice conversion with minimal delay\n* **CPU-optimized**: Efficient enough to run on CPU in real-time\n* **Streaming support**: True streaming inference with chunked processing\n* **High quality**: Natural voice conversion while maintaining low latency\n* **Compatible architecture**: Based on RVC/QuickVC with optimizations\n* **Small model size**: Low resource requirements for edge deployment\n* **No F0 dependency**: Optional pitch-independent conversion mode\n* **MIT License**: Free for commercial use\n\nLLVC achieves real-time factor (RTF) < 0.1 on CPU, making it suitable for live applications like real-time dubbing, streaming, gaming voice chat, and interactive voice applications.\n\nThe goal is to enable this model to run on TT hardware for ultra-high-throughput, ultra-low-latency voice conversion optimized for real-time applications.\n\n\n### 🎯 What Success Looks Like\n\nA successful submission will fulfill all requirements in the following stages. Payout is made after all three stages are completed.\n\n\n### Stage 1 — Bring-Up\n\n* Implement LLVC using TTNN APIs (Python)\n* Implements the full generation pipeline:\n  * Lightweight encoder (optimized for low latency)\n  * Streaming-capable architecture\n  * Efficient decoder\n  * Optional pitch extraction (F0-based and F0-free modes)\n  * Vocoder integration\n* Model runs on either N150 or N300 Tenstorrent hardware with no errors\n* Supports both modes:\n  * **Streaming mode**: Real-time conversion with chunked processing\n  * **Non-streaming mode**: Full-context conversion\n* Produces valid converted audio output\n* Output is verifiable (audio quality assessment, compare with PyTorch reference)\n* Achieves baseline throughput target:\n  * At least 50 tokens/second for decoder generation\n  * Real-time factor (RTF) < 0.3 for streaming mode\n  * Latency < 100ms for streaming chunks\n* Accuracy evaluation:\n  * Speaker similarity > 70% (cosine similarity)\n  * Content preservation: WER < 3.0\n  * Token-level accuracy > 95% against PyTorch reference\n* Audio quality: Natural prosody with minimal artifacts despite low latency\n* Clear instructions for setup and running the model\n\n### Stage 2 — Basic Optimizations\n\n* Use optimal sharded/interleaved memory configs for encoder-decoder layers\n* Implement efficient sharding strategy for:\n  * Lightweight encoder layers\n  * Decoder layers optimized for streaming\n  * Convolutional layers with causal padding\n  * Cached convolution states for streaming\n  * Optional pitch extraction module\n* Fuse simple ops where possible (e.g., layer normalization, activation functions)\n* Store intermediate activations in L1 where beneficial\n* Use recommended TTNN/tt-metal flows for streaming audio models\n* Leverage TT library of fused ops for convolution blocks\n* Optimize chunk-based processing for streaming\n* Efficient state management for causal convolutions\n* Optimize vocoder integration\n\n### Stage 3 — Deeper Optimization\n\n* Maximize core counts used per inference\n* Implement deeper TT-specific optimizations:\n  * Ultra-low latency streaming (minimize chunk processing time)\n  * Efficient causal convolution with state caching\n  * Flash Attention or equivalent where applicable\n  * Minimize voice conversion latency per chunk\n  * Batch processing for multiple concurrent streams\n  * Pipeline encoder/decoder/vocoder stages\n  * Optimize memory footprint for edge deployment\n* Minimize memory and TM (tensor manipulation) overheads\n* Explore look-ahead strategies for quality vs latency trade-off\n* Document any advanced tuning, known limitations, or trade-offs\n* Target stretched goals:\n  * 100+ tokens/second generation speed\n  * RTF < 0.1 for streaming mode (match CPU performance)\n  * Latency < 50ms for streaming chunks\n  * Support for 10+ concurrent streams\n\n### 🧭 Guidance & Starting Points\n\n* Use the [TTNN model bring-up tech report](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/tech_reports/ttnn/TTNN-model-bringup.md) as your primary reference\n* Reference [streaming audio model patterns in tt-metal](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/main/models/demos) for streaming architectures\n* Use the [official LLVC repository](https://github.com/KoeAI/LLVC) for model architecture details\n* Refer to the [LLVC paper (arXiv:2311.00873)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.00873) for technical details\n* Check [LLVC demo page](https://koeai.github.io/llvc-demo/) for audio samples\n* Refer to [TT Fused ops PR #29236](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/pull/29236) for optimization opportunities\n* The model architecture consists of:\n  * **Lightweight encoder**: Optimized convolutional layers with reduced complexity\n  * **Cached convolutions**: State management for causal streaming inference\n  * **Efficient decoder**: Minimal layers for low latency\n  * **Optional F0 module**: Pitch extraction when needed\n  * **Vocoder**: HiFi-GAN or similar (can be shared with other models)\n* Key challenges:\n  * Ultra-low latency requirements (< 100ms)\n  * Streaming inference with causal convolutions\n  * State management across chunks\n  * Quality vs latency trade-off\n  * Vocoder integration and optimization\n  * Small model size constraints\n* Streaming parameters:\n  * `window_ms`: Chunk size in milliseconds (affects latency)\n  * `extra_convert_size`: Extra context for quality (affects latency)\n* Ask for help or file issues if ops are missing in TTNN\n\n\n### 🔎 Possible Approaches\n\n* Start from the [official LLVC repository](https://github.com/KoeAI/LLVC) and port components sequentially:\n  1. Lightweight encoder (optimized convolutions)\n  2. Cached convolution layers for streaming\n  3. Efficient decoder\n  4. Optional pitch extraction (F0 mode)\n  5. Vocoder integration\n  6. Streaming inference pipeline with state management\n* Validate each submodule's output against PyTorch reference before integration\n* Experiment with different sharding strategies:\n  * Channel sharding for convolutions\n  * Sequence length sharding for chunks\n  * Minimize cross-chip communication\n* Use TTNN profiling tools to identify bottlenecks in:\n  * Per-chunk processing time (critical metric)\n  * Encoder latency\n  * Decoder latency\n  * State management overhead\n  * Vocoder latency\n* Test diverse use cases:\n  * Streaming mode with various chunk sizes (50ms, 100ms, 200ms)\n  * Non-streaming mode for comparison\n  * F0-based vs F0-free modes\n  * Multiple concurrent streams\n  * Real-time conversion scenarios\n* Open a draft PR early to get feedback on your approach\n\n\n\n## 📊 Result Submission Guidelines\n\nBeyond the model implementation itself, contributors must submit the following material as proof of work.\nHowever, feel free to open a PR at any time if you want us checking that you are on the right track.\nJust understand that payout is only made after **all 3 stages** are completed.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Functional model implementation\n- Validation logs (output correctness)\n- Performance report + header for final review\n\n**Links:**\n- [Performance Sheet](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/tech_reports/ttnn/TTNN-model-bringup.md#41-performance-sheet)\n- [Perf Header Docs](https://docs.tenstorrent.com/tt-metal/latest/ttnn/ttnn/profiling_ttnn_operations.html#perf-report-headers)\n\n\n### 📚 Resources\n\n### Model Resources\n\n* [LLVC Official Repository](https://github.com/KoeAI/LLVC)\n* [LLVC Paper (arXiv:2311.00873)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.00873)\n* [LLVC Demo Page](https://koeai.github.io/llvc-demo/)\n* [LLVC Paper PDF](https://koe.ai/papers/llvc.pdf)\n* [Koe AI Homepage](https://koe.ai/)\n* [RVC Repository (related)](https://github.com/RVC-Project/Retrieval-based-Voice-Conversion-WebUI)\n\n### TT-Metal Resources\n\n* [TTNN Model Bring-up Tech Report](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/tech_reports/ttnn/TTNN-model-bringup.md)\n* [Streaming Audio Models in tt-metal](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/main/models/demos)\n* [TT Fused Ops PR #29236](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/pull/29236)\n* [Performance Report Header](https://docs.tenstorrent.com/tt-metal/latest/ttnn/ttnn/profiling_ttnn_operations.html#perf-report-headers)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/32187/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/32187/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/events","html_url":"https://github.com/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103","id":4825321319,"node_id":"I_kwDOTKH7388AAAABH5yPZw","number":103,"title":"Tower Rework + closing rebalance: five newcomer kits, two engine systems, full retune (developer-ratified 2026-07-07)","user":{"login":"TaySchub","id":298097911,"node_id":"U_kgDOEcSc9w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298097911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub","html_url":"https://github.com/TaySchub","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-07-07T04:47:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:08:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Developer-ratified 2026-07-07** (tower-by-tower review session; final rulings at session close: syrup PURE CONTROL confirmed · MAPLE SYRUP confirmed · JUICE LAYER VETOED — mechanics only, standard presentation).\n\nThe \"game feels stale\" fix, tower side (dishes side = #98). ONE PR in THREE staged commits (developer decision, second session: the closing rebalance is folded in as stage 3 rather than a separate PR — formerly #104, closed as superseded): stage 1 builds the two shared engine systems inert, stage 2 reworks the five newcomer kits, stage 3 is the closing rebalance. The kits:\n\n- **Pitmaster** — Path A: faster stacking + cap 5→8 (t1), ambient smoke AURA (t2). Path B: +range (t1), cooks 2 dishes at once (t2, count frozen).\n- **Ranch → \"The Syrup Slinger\"** (display rename only; internal id `ranch` frozen forever) — cone + coats deleted; new base = single-target maple-syrup glob → immediate full glue-slow, **pure control, zero damage**. Path A: faster slinging (t1), Syrup Trail belt puddle (t2, glues up to 3 — frozen). Path B: +range (t1), globs 3 at once (t2, frozen). Fence: Photographer owns the hard STOP, syrup owns the long DRAG.\n- **Sample Lady** — full rework to **pure support, no attack** (sampling stays as flavor animation). Base aura: nearby towers attack faster + upgrades cost 10% less (discounted price shown in the sheet). Path A: +radius (t1), +damage in aura (t2). Path B: value-tag dishes (t1), haste stacks further (t2).\n- **Short-Order Cook** — Seasoned Griddle t2 knockback-chance deleted (kills the only newcomer RNG signature) → \"Stove on High\" = pure big damage add. Everything else kept.\n- **Competitive Eater** — Solomon Method + Mustard Belt + combo-cap effects deleted; combo stays base-only. Path A: faster → much faster (cooldown-floor guard). Path B: +damage per bite → tip-jackpot per kill, priced expensive.\n\n**New engine systems** (the layer future content inherits): (1) enemy-side ZONE applicators — ambient aura + belt puddle, one system, two shapes; (2) TOWER-PROXIMITY support effects — one radius check → haste / +damage / upgrade-discount.\n\n**Stages 1–2 ship shelf values; stage 3 is the closing rebalance** (numbers-only, the only stage where the gate legitimately moves): prices the reworked kits against the current four dishes, re-holds every BALANCE_PHILOSOPHY §4 bar, re-verifies the Slurper fence (unfed Eater DPS strictly below Slurper's unconditional DPS), and prices the premium tiers premium. **ORDER FLIP (developer decision 2026-07-07): this PR runs BEFORE #98** — the dishes land afterward and get priced against these kits by #98's own retune stage.\n\n**Save guarantee (developer-ratified, second session 2026-07-07):** a player's save must NEVER break — this PR deletes upgrade paths that live inside serialized checkpoints, so restore MIGRATES (orphaned tiers refunded at full value into the run) rather than discarding; a garbage save can never brick boot. Details in the kickoff.\n\n**Blocked on:** nothing — READY TO RUN (prereq: origin/main post-#102, 10 towers in balance.json).\n**Review tier (docs/CHECKPOINT.md, top tier):** checkpoint before merge **+ the developer runs `/code-review ultra <PR#>`** on the open PR — new engine systems + a save-compatibility touch, and the first big engine PR post-Fable.\n**Sequencing after:** #98 Menu Expansion (its retune prices the dishes against these kits) → audio pass 2 (#64: sounds for the new verbs — glob/splat, aura sizzle, bell) → Pizzeria (#39).\n\nKickoff prompt in the first comment.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/events","html_url":"https://github.com/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98","id":4824842243,"node_id":"I_kwDOTKH7388AAAABH5VAAw","number":98,"title":"Menu Expansion: three new dishes (enemy variety for the 10-tower roster)","user":{"login":"TaySchub","id":298097911,"node_id":"U_kgDOEcSc9w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298097911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub","html_url":"https://github.com/TaySchub","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11384592958,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTKH7388AAAACppMaPg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/labels/feature","name":"feature","color":"48ebb5","default":false,"description":"New functionality"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-07T03:04:54Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:08:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The roster doubled but the belt still serves the same FOUR dishes — enemy variety is the other half of the staleness fix (tower-upgrade review is happening separately with the developer). THREE new foods as stat+art archetypes only (ultra-fast glass-cannon / awkward mid-tank / rare premium high-bounty plate — builder's designs within those lanes): zero new engine mechanics (splitter stays reserved for Map 2 #39), silhouette-first no-face dish art with bite states, staged waveGen introduction.\n\nUnlike the tower pipeline, this PR **legitimately moves the gate** → stage 2 re-holds every BALANCE_PHILOSOPHY §4 bar (gate 50–60 aim ~55, ≥52 at CI config, engagement/pacing/spam/recoverability) and must show each new dish creates pressure the old four didn't.\n\n**Hard prereq: PR #97 (menu + rename) merged first.** Opus 4.8 high effort, runs in parallel with the developer's tower-by-tower upgrade review (disjoint: dishes vs tower kits). **Fable checkpoint before merge** (gate-moving). Kickoff: first comment below.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5","id":4148310877,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjNd","number":5,"title":"[BOUNTY $200] WORKFLOW: n8n + Claude Code — automated weekly dev summary","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402738,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e2Mg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/workflow","name":"workflow","color":"0891B2","default":false,"description":"Automation workflow"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":828,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:44Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:01:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $200 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate a complete n8n workflow that automatically generates a weekly narrative\nsummary of a GitHub repo's activity, using the Claude API.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exportable n8n workflow (importable `.json` file)\n- [ ] Trigger: weekly cron (e.g., Friday at 5pm)\n- [ ] Fetches from GitHub API: commits, closed issues, merged PRs for the week\n- [ ] Calls Claude API (`claude-sonnet-4-20250514`) to generate a narrative summary\n- [ ] Delivers the summary via: email OR Discord/Slack webhook (your choice, documented)\n- [ ] Configurable variables: GitHub repo, destination channel, language (EN/FR)\n- [ ] Tested on a real n8n instance (include a screenshot of successful execution)\n- [ ] README with setup instructions in 5 steps or fewer\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with the `.json` workflow + README\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅\n\n## Resources\n- n8n docs: https://docs.n8n.io\n- Claude API docs: https://docs.anthropic.com","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/5/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5924","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5924/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5924/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5924/events","html_url":"https://github.com/devpool-directory/devpool-directory/issues/5924","id":3885310528,"node_id":"I_kwDOJWyCVM7nlSJA","number":5924,"title":"Launch Another DoraHacks Bounty Post","user":{"login":"devpool-directory-superintendent