cked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Update the benchmark suite and bring it into the CI runner [$400]\r\n\r\nQuantumOptics.jl has an in-depth benchmarking suite that has bitrotted in the last few years. To claim this bounty:\r\n\r\n- Set up a benchmark-on-CI infrastructure (e.g. similar to the one in QuantumClifford.jl) that runs QuantumOptics-specific benchmarks on each pull request\r\n- Include all old benchmarks in that infrastructure (reusing the existing benchmark suite as much as possible) and make it easy to add new micro-benchmarks as new features get developed.\r\n\r\nThe above are for the sake of the developers of this package. However, this bounty also requires the following to be done for the sake of users:\r\n\r\n- Fix up the capability to run benchmarks in comparison to popular python packages (qutip) and add comparative Julia packages (QuantumToolbox.jl)\r\n- Create a makefile that let's a developer to easily update the webpage presenting these comparative benchmarks to the user.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Understanding of Julia's and Python's benchmarking infrastructure.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov and/or @david-pl \r\n\r\n**Duration**: 2 months\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377","id":4825275259,"node_id":"I_kwDOAjHKnc8AAAABH5vbew","number":9377,"title":"Add-on submission: Disclosure Contact Lookup (disclose/zap-lookup)","user":{"login":"yesnet0","id":12779999,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzc5OTk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12779999?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0","html_url":"https://github.com/yesnet0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-07T04:37:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T04:37:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Submitting a new third-party add-on for the ZAP Marketplace.\n\n### Add-on repo\nhttps://github.com/disclose/zap-lookup\n\n### Your contact details\nhello@disclose.io — a [disclose.io](https://disclose.io) project (an open, vendor-neutral nonprofit for vulnerability disclosure).\n\n### Are you one of the authors?\nYes.\n\n### License\nMIT (see `LICENSE`).\n\n### Build instructions\n`gradle jarZapAddOn` (JDK 17, Gradle 8.13+). CI builds the `.zap` on every push (`.github/workflows/build.yml`), and a prebuilt `.zap` is attached to the [v1.0.0 release](https://github.com/disclose/zap-lookup/releases/tag/v1.0.0).\n\n### Link for more information\n- Repo / README: https://github.com/disclose/zap-lookup\n- The attribution API it calls: https://lookup.disclose.io\n\n### What it does\n**Disclosure Contact Lookup** adds a right-click **“Find disclosure contact”** menu item on any HTTP message. It resolves the selected host to its owning organization and a ranked list of security-disclosure channels (security.txt, VDP / bug-bounty programs, PSIRT directories) via the free [lookup.disclose.io](https://lookup.disclose.io) attribution API — so a tester knows exactly where to report a finding. It’s the open-source-proxy sibling of the disclose.io Burp and Caido extensions.\n\n**Privacy / safety:** it sends only the *host string* (e.g. `github.com`) — never request/response content — and makes only that one read-only outbound call. No scan traffic, no writes.\n\n### Status\nAlpha (first release). Add-on id `zap-lookup`, package `io.disclose.zaplookup`, min ZAP version 2.16.0. Verified: builds in CI, and loads cleanly in ZAP 2.17.0 (the extension initializes with no errors).\n\n### Promote to Beta or Release?\nNo — start at Alpha.\n\n### Anything else we should know?\nHappy to add an integrated help file or address any review feedback.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743/events","html_url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/743","id":4530092639,"node_id":"I_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABDgO6Xw","number":743,"title":"Low Handing Fruit Automation","user":{"login":"claim-reviewer","id":72201398,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjAxMzk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72201398?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer","html_url":"https://github.com/claim-reviewer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claim-reviewer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10969608408,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjdbw2A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":10969608412,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjdbw3A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Improvements or additions to documentation"},{"id":10969608427,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjdbw6w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":10969608431,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjdbw7w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/help%20wanted","name":"help wanted","color":"008672","default":true,"description":"Extra attention is needed"},{"id":10969735624,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjdjhyA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":""},{"id":10970651882,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjebc6g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/AI%20agent%20friendly","name":"AI agent friendly","color":"e69469","default":false,"description":""},{"id":10970655211,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjebp6w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"cafa53","default":false,"description":""},{"id":10970820972,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACjelxbA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/%F0%9F%92%8E%20Bounty","name":"💎 Bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11064514169,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSfPzA88AAAACk38WeQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/labels/$700","name":"$700","color":"34d399","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1377,"created_at":"2026-05-27T06:32:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T04:15:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Automate Low Hanging fruit bug detection and issue creation recursively.\n\nThis issue is an issue focused on creating more issues:\n1. Find a feature/bug to work on from this repository\n2. Create a GitHub issue on the repository to start working on it -- Pull requests without issues will not be considered.\n3. Use the following string in the issue that you created: \"This issue is limited only to the creator of this issue. This means that only the issue author can attempt to solve this issue. If you would like to work on it, please create another issue with the same contents and refer to issue #743 for more information.\"\n\nFollow all instructions carefully and precisely.\n\n/bounty $700\n\nBounties can only be paid upon successful PR merge.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.gi