m/users/Julesssss/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Julesssss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Julesssss/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Julesssss/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Julesssss/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Julesssss/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Julesssss/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/77171","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Run a Knip audit to identify and remove unused files, exports, and dependencies across the codebase.\n\n```\n## All listed items per section\n\n| Section | Count |\n|---------|-------|\n| Unlisted binaries | 1 |\n| Unlisted dependencies | 161 |\n| Unused dependencies | 1 |\n| Unused devDependencies | 1 |\n| Unused exported types | 162 |\n| Unused exports | 128 |\n| Unused files | 64 |\n\n```\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Issue Owner</summary>Current Issue Owner: @QichenZhu</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/86254/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/86254/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2782","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2782/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2782/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2782/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2782","id":4195435600,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa876EURQ","number":2782,"title":"[ONBOARD: 1 RTC] Review an Open PR","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029430,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZtg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10360962887,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACaY-_Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/onboarding","name":"onboarding","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1358,"created_at":"2026-04-02T15:41:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T03:16:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 2 RTC\n\n### What You'll Do\nHelp us review code. Every PR benefits from a second pair of eyes.\n\n### Steps\n1. **Pick any open PR** from [Rustchain](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pulls), [BoTTube](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/pulls), or [rustchain-bounties](https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/pulls)\n2. **Read the code changes** (click \"Files changed\" tab)\n3. **Leave a substantive review comment**. Examples:\n   - \"Line 42: this SQL query isn't parameterized, potential injection\"\n   - \"This function duplicates logic already in utils.py line 80\"\n   - \"Missing error handling if the API returns non-200\"\n   - \"Good approach, but the variable name should describe what it holds\"\n4. **Comment here** with a link to your review\n\n### What Counts\n- Review must be **technical and specific** (not \"looks good\" or \"nice work\")\n- Point to specific lines with specific observations\n- Positive observations count too (\"good use of context manager here\")\n- You don't need to be an expert. Asking good questions is reviewing.\n\n### Payment\n2 RTC once your review contains at least 2 substantive observations.\n\n**Difficulty**: Easy-Medium | **Time**: 20-40 min | **Skills**: Can read Python or JavaScript\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2782/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":3,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2782/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29100","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29100/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29100/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29100/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29100","id":4002626231,"node_id":"I_kwDOQb6kR87ukzq3","number":29100,"title":"[Feature]: Cost metadata support for auto-discovered Amazon Bedrock models","user":{"login":"mg-mavios","id":163306920,"node_id":"U_kgDOCbvdqA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163306920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios","html_url":"https://github.com/mg-mavios","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mg-mavios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9706244996,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACQomLhA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"0969DA","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"},{"id":10970446441,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACjeO6aQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/P2","name":"P2","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":"Normal backlog priority with limited blast radius."},{"id":10971435209,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACjfLQyQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/clawsweeper:no-new-fix-pr","name":"clawsweeper:no-new-fix-pr","color":"E5E7EB","default":false,"description":"ClawSweeper does not recommend queueing a new automated fix PR for this issue."},{"id":10971435625,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACjfLSaQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/clawsweeper:needs-maintainer-review","name":"clawsweeper:needs-maintainer-review","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":"ClawSweeper marked this issue as needing maintainer review before automation."},{"id":10971435771,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACjfLS-w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/clawsweeper:needs-product-decision","name":"clawsweeper:needs-product-decision","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":"ClawSweeper marked this issue as needing a product or behavior decision."},{"id":10971438267,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACjfLcuw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/clawsweeper:source-repro","name":"clawsweeper:source-repro","color":"0A3069","default":false,"description":"ClawSweeper found a high-confidence source-level issue reproduction."},{"id":10973514562,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACjhKLQg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/impact:auth-provider","name":"impact:auth-provider","color":"F9D65C","default":false,"description":"Auth, provider routing, model choice, or SecretRef resolution may break."},{"id":10981171401,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACjodgyQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/labels/issue-rating:%20%F0%9F%A6%9E%20diamond%20lobster","name":"issue-rating: 🦞 diamond lobster","color":"0969DA","default":false,"description":"Very strong issue quality with high-confidence source-level or clear reproduction."}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-02-27T19:54:59Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:48:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Summary\n\nAllow cost-per-token metadata to be attached to Bedrock models discovered via models.bedrockDiscovery without requiring a duplicate explicit provider block.\n\n### Problem to solve\n\nWhen using Amazon Bedrock with IAM role-based auto-discovery (models.bedrockDiscovery), there is no supported way to attach cost metadata (input, output, cacheRead, cacheWrite) to discovered models. Cost config is only supported via explicit models.providers.<provider>.models[] entries, which requires duplicating the entire provider block just to add pricing — conflicting with the auto-discovery pattern and creating config redundancy. As a result, /status and /usage show token counts only with no USD estimates for Bedrock users on IAM auth.\n\n### Proposed solution\n\nAdd a `costs` map to `models.bedrockDiscovery` keyed by model ID:\n\n```json5\n{\n  models: {\n    bedrockDiscovery: {\n      enabled: true,\n      costs: {\n        \"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\": { input: 3, output: 15, cacheRead: 0.3, cacheWrite: 3.75 },\n        \"us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\": { input: 1, output: 5, cacheRead: 0.1, cacheWrite: 1.25 }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, a top-level `models.costs` map that patches cost onto any model by ID regardless of discovery method would be a more general solution covering other auto-discovered providers in the future.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\nDefining an explicit models.providers.amazon-bedrock block solely to carry cost metadata while IAM role auth continues via auto-discovery. This works but creates a hybrid config that is confusing, hard to maintain, and requires manually listing models that are otherwise managed automatically.\n\n### Impact\n\nAffected: Any OpenClaw deployment using Bedrock with IAM role / instance profile auth (common in EC2/ECS/cloud deployments)\nSeverity: Medium — blocks cost visibility, important for multi-agent setups where sub-agents accumulate token usage across parallel runs\nFrequency: Every session — cost estimates are never shown for Bedrock auto-discovered models\nConsequence: Operators cannot monitor spend, cannot compare per-agent costs, and cannot make informed model tier decisions without external tooling\n\n### Evidence/examples\n\nConfirmed via local docs (/providers/bedrock.md, /reference/token-use.md): bedrockDiscovery config accepts defaultContextWindow and defaultMaxTokens but no cost fields. The cost field is only documented under models.providers.<provider>.models[].\n\n### Additional information\n\nSolution must remain backward-compatible with existing bedrockDiscovery config and should not require AWS credentials or model access beyond what auto-discovery already uses. The costs map should be a pure overlay — no behavioral changes, only metadata enrichment for billing display.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29100/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/29100/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71","id":3904303864,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87otvL4","number":71,"title":"[BOUNTY] Ongoing Bug Bounty Program — Find Bugs, Earn RTC (133 RTC Pool)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029408,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZoA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/open","name":"open","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Open for claims"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":432,"created_at":"2026-02-06T01:13:53Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:47:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Ongoing Bug Bounty Program\n\n**Pool: 750 RTC (ongoing, replenished as needed)**\n\n### Severity & Rewards\n| Severity | Description | Reward |\n|----------|-------------|--------|\n| **Critical** | Fund theft, consensus bypass, RCE | 100-200 RTC |\n| **High** | Data leak, auth bypass, significant logic error | 50-100 RTC |\n| **Medium** | DoS, info disclosure, moderate bugs | 15-50 RTC |\n| **Low** | UI bugs, minor leaks, doc errors | 5-15 RTC |\n\n### In-Scope\n- RustChain node software, attestation & fingerprint system\n- Epoch settlement & rewards, wallet endpoints\n- BoTTube web app, API, payment system\n- Python SDK, Block Explorer, Wallet GUI, Miner clients\n\n### Reporting\n1. Create GitHub issue with `[SECURITY]` prefix\n2. For critical: email first, issue after fix\n3. Include: steps to reproduce, impact, suggested fix\n\n### Rules\n- First reporter wins\n- Responsible disclosure required\n- Must not exploit on production\n\n---\n*Total RTC supply: 8.3M | RTC Reference Rate: 1 RTC = $0.10 USD*","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":3,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455","id":4002331192,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87ujro4","number":455,"title":"[25 RTC] Dual-Mining: Ergo (Autolykos2) Integration","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":14,"created_at":"2026-02-27T18:34:38Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:35:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Ergo Dual-Mining Integration — 25 RTC\n\n**Mine Ergo + earn RTC for free.** RIP-PoA attestation costs zero compute.\n\n### What to Build\n\nImplement and test the Ergo-specific proof path in `clawrtc/data/pow_miners.py`:\n\n1. **Node RPC proof** (1.5x bonus): Query local Ergo node at `localhost:9053/info` — verify `isMining: true`, extract chain height, peer count, best block hash\n2. **Pool account proof** (1.3x bonus): Verify hashrate via HeroMiners, WoolyPooly, Nanopool, or 2miners API\n3. **Server validation**: Add Ergo-specific validation in `validate_pow_proof()` on the RustChain node\n\n### Ergo Node API Reference\n- `GET /info` — node status, mining flag, height\n- `GET /mining/candidate` — current mining candidate (proves active mining)\n- Default port: 9053 (mainnet), 9052 (testnet)\n\n### Testing\n- Run an Ergo node with mining enabled\n- Run `clawrtc mine --pow ergo`\n- Verify proof is generated and accepted by RustChain node\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Ergo node auto-detected by port + process\n- [ ] Node RPC proof includes chain height + mining status\n- [ ] Pool verification works for at least 2 pools\n- [ ] Nonce binding prevents proof replay\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n\nSee master issue: #453","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781","id":4195434807,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa876EUE3","number":2781,"title":"[ONBOARD: 1 RTC] File Your First Bug Report","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029430,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZtg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10360962887,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACaY-_Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/onboarding","name":"onboarding","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":237,"created_at":"2026-04-02T15:41:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:07:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 1 RTC\n\n### What You'll Do\nGet familiar with RustChain by exploring the codebase and reporting something real.\n\n### Steps\n1. **Explore** the README, docs, or try running the miner in `--dry-run` mode\n2. **File a bug report** on [Rustchain issues](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues). This can be:\n   - A broken link you found\n   - A confusing error message\n   - A doc section that confused you as a newcomer\n   - An actual bug\n3. **Comment here** with a link to your issue\n\n### What Counts\n- The issue must be **real and specific** (not \"the docs could be better\")\n- Duplicate issues don't count, check existing issues first\n- Your fresh-eyes perspective is genuinely valuable. Newcomers find things veterans miss.\n\n### Payment\n1 RTC once your issue is verified as a real finding.\n\n### Why This Exists\nEvery open-source project needs fresh eyes. Your first contribution starts with looking at the code and telling us what's broken or confusing.\n\n**Difficulty**: Easy | **Time**: 15-30 min | **Skills**: Reading comprehension\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":2,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/events","html_url":"https://github.com/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7","id":4525015280,"node_id":"I_kwDOSkrEes8AAAABDbZA8A","number":7,"title":"🚨 Zero Day Pulse — Active Vulnerability Tracker","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11025306354,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSkrEes8AAAACkSjS8g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/labels/zero-day-pulse","name":"zero-day-pulse","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":168,"created_at":"2026-05-26T14:37:26Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:00:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Zero Day Pulse\n\n> **Generated:** 2026-05-26 14:37 UTC &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Total:** 15 &nbsp;|&nbsp; 🔴 KEV: 0 &nbsp;|&nbsp; 🟠 Zero-Day: 13 &nbsp;|&nbsp; 🟡 High: 2 &nbsp;|&nbsp; ✨ Enriched: 10\n\n---\n\n## 1. 🟠 Zero-Day — Ransomware Actors Exploit Unpatched SimpleHelp Remote Monitoring and Management to Compromise Utility Billing Software Provider\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2024-57727` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** CISA US-CERT Alerts &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** Thu, 12 Ju\n**Reference:** <https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-163a>\n\n> Summary The Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) is releasing this advisory in response to ransomware actors leveraging unpatched instances of a vulnerability in SimpleHelp Remote Monitoring and Management (RMM) to compromise customers of a utility billing software provider. This incident reflects a broader pattern of ransomware actors targeting organizations through unpatched v…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** CVE-2024-57727 is a path traversal vulnerability in SimpleHelp (v5.5.7 and earlier) enabling unauthenticated attackers to retrieve logs, configuration files, credentials and potentially gain access to downstream systems.\n- **Affected Products:** SimpleHelp remote support software v5.5.7 and earlier\n- **CVSS Score:** 7.5\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable\n- **Exploit Available:** true (https://medium.com/@RosanaFS/simplehelp-cve-2024-57727-tryhackme-walkthrough-9f88c2061fb9)\n- **Patch Available:** true (http://community.simple-help.com/t/simplehelp-5-5-8-critical-security-fixes/1570)\n- **Active Exploitation:** true (https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-163a)\n- **Threat Actors:** Ransomware actors (e.g., DragonForce)\n- **Mitigation:** Apply vendor patch to v5.5.8 immediately; if unable, isolate SimpleHelp RMM from internet, restrict access to management interfaces, apply network segmentation, rotate exposed credentials, enable logging and monitoring, and follow CISA incident response guidance.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://simple-help.com/blogs/security-vulnerabilities-in-simplehelp-5-5-7-and-earlier-what-you-need-to-know\n\n---\n\n## 2. 🟠 Zero-Day — Hackers Exploited KnowledgeDeliver Zero-Day for Web Shell Deployment\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** SecurityWeek &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://www.securityweek.com/hackers-exploited-knowledgedeliver-zero-day-for-web-shell-deployment/>\n\n> Hardcoded machineKey values in a configuration file enabled ViewState deserialization attacks leading to remote code execution. The post Hackers Exploited KnowledgeDeliver Zero-Day for Web Shell Deployment appeared first on SecurityWeek .\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Hard‑coded ASP.NET machineKey values enable attackers who obtain the key to create malicious __VIEWSTATE payloads that bypass validation, causing deserialization and unauthenticated remote code execution; the breach culminates in deployment of in‑memory BLUEBEAM (Godzilla) web shells.\n- **Affected Products:** Digital Knowledge KnowledgeDeliver (installations deployed before Feb 24, 2026)\n- **CVSS Score:** 7.5\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N\n- **Exploit Available:** true\n- **Patch Available:** true\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** Unknown specific group; Mandiant reports an \"unknown threat actor\"\n- **Mitigation:** Immediately rotate machineKey to unique cryptographically strong values per instance; restrict external access (IP allowlist); monitor Event ID 1316 and ViewState integrity failures, and hunt for suspicious w3wp.exe child processes and related IOCs.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** Vendor advisory URL unavailable.\n\n---\n\n## 3. 🟠 Zero-Day — Iranian Hackers Deploy MiniFast and MiniJunk V2 via Phishing and SEO Poisoning\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** The Hacker News Security &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/iranian-hackers-deploy-minifast-and.html>\n\n> The Iranian state-sponsored threat actor known as Nimbus Manticore (aka Screening Serpens and UNC1549) has been attributed to a fresh campaign using lures impersonating organizations in the aviation and software sectors across the U.S., Europe, and the Middle East following the joint U.S.-Israeli military campaign against the country in late February 2026.\n\nThe activity, besides embracing\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Campaigns use SEO poisoning and spear/phishing lures to deliver MiniFast (AI‑assisted) and MiniJunk V2 implants. Delivery vectors include malicious links and attachments; implants perform espionage (recon, credential harvesting, persistence) and likely leverage cloud services (reported abuse of Microsoft Azure) for hosting C2 and payloads.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable.\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** false\n- **Patch Available:** false\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** Nimbus Manticore (aka Screening Serpens, UNC1549)\n- **Mitigation:** Increase email security and phishing awareness; block known malicious domains and SEO‑poisoned landing pages; implement URL filtering and web proxying; enable EDR/anti‑malware with YARA/signature and behavior detections; disable/limit macros and script execution; apply least‑privilege and multi‑factor authentication; isolate and investigate suspected hosts.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** Vendor advisory URL unavailable.\n\n---\n\n## 4. 🟠 Zero-Day — AI threats in the wild: The current state of prompt injections on the web\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-04-23\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/ai-threats-in-wild-current-state-of.html>\n\n> Posted by Thomas Brunner, Yu-Han Liu, Moni Pande At Google, our Threat Intelligence teams are dedicated to staying ahead of real-world adversarial activity, proactively monitoring emerging threats before they can impact users. Right now, Indirect Prompt Injection (IPI) is a top priority for the security community, anticipating it as a primary attack vector for adversaries to target and compromise …\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Indirect Prompt Injection (IPI) occurs when adversarial content hosted on public web pages or other untrusted sources contains instructions or payloads that an LLM‑powered agent ingests as part of its context, causing it to execute unintended actions (data exfiltration, API key theft, command execution via agent frameworks). Attack vectors include crafted web pages, embedded comments, README files, or other content that agents fetch when following web browsing or tool‑use capabilities.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** true — https://www.forcepoint.com/blog/x-labs/indirect-prompt-injection-payloads\n- **Patch Available:** false — https://microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/05/07/prompts-become-shells-rce-vulnerabilities-ai-agent-frameworks\n- **Active Exploitation:** true — Sources: https://www.forcepoint.com/blog/x-labs/indirect-prompt-injection-payloads, http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/ai-threats-in-wild-current-state-of.html\n- **Threat Actors:** None known\n- **Mitigation:** Implement input provenance controls, remote content filtering, strict instruction parsing, principle of least privilege for agents, sanitize and ignore untrusted web-origin instructions, use model grounding and instruction allowlists/denylists, robust content security policies.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/ai-threats-in-wild-current-state-of.html\n\n---\n\n## 5. 🟠 Zero-Day — Google Workspace’s continuous approach to mitigating indirect prompt injections\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-04-02\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/google-workspaces-continuous-approach.html>\n\n> Posted by Adam Gavish, Google GenAI Security Team Indirect prompt injection (IPI) is an evolving threat vector targeting users of complex AI applications with multiple data sources, such as Workspace with Gemini. This technique enables the attacker to influence the behavior of an LLM by injecting malicious instructions into the data or tools used by the LLM as it completes the user’s query. This m…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Indirect prompt injection (IPI) exploits the ability of large language models to consume data from multiple sources. By inserting crafted malicious instructions into those sources or associated tools, an attacker can steer the model’s output or actions even when the user does not directly provide malicious input.\n- **Affected Products:** Google Workspace (Gemini), Gemini CLI\n- **CVSS Score:** 10.0\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** Exploit availability unknown.\n- **Patch Available:** true\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** Threat actors unknown.\n- **Mitigation:** Apply the latest Google Workspace and Gemini CLI patches, enable Google’s continuous mitigation controls, monitor logs for anomalous prompt activity, and restrict the use of automated agents that can ingest untrusted data.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/google-workspaces-continuous-approach.html\n\n---\n\n## 6. 🟠 Zero-Day — Architecting Security for Agentic Capabilities in Chrome\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2025-12-08\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2025/12/architecting-security-for-agentic.html>\n\n> Posted by Nathan Parker, Chrome security team Chrome has been advancing the web’s security for well over 15 years, and we’re committed to meeting new challenges and opportunities with AI. Billions of people trust Chrome to keep them safe by default, and this is a responsibility we take seriously. Following the recent launch of Gemini in Chrome and the preview of agentic capabilities , we want to s…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Chrome's agentic features face \"indirect prompt injection\": malicious instructions embedded in web content (pages, iframes, UGC) can influence an agent to perform unwanted actions (e.g., transactions, exfiltration). Google describes layered defenses: origin gating, a User Alignment Critic classifier, planner/gating function separation, explicit user confirmations for sensitive actions, Safe Browsing and on‑device scam detection, and work‑logs for transparency.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable.\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** false.\n- **Patch Available:** true; https://blog.google/security/architecting-security-for-agentic/\n- **Active Exploitation:** false.\n- **Threat Actors:** None known.\n- **Mitigation:** Use Google’s layered defenses and hardening: enable the latest Chrome updates with agentic protections; rely on origin gating and user confirmations; monitor Safe Browsing and on‑device protections; follow Google guidance in the vendor advisory; consider blocking agentic browsers in high‑risk environments per Gartner/NCSC guidance.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** https://blog.google/security/architecting-security-for-agentic/\n\n---\n\n## 7. 🟠 Zero-Day — Rust in Android: move fast and fix things\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2025-11-13\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2025/11/rust-in-android-move-fast-fix-things.html>\n\n> Posted by Jeff Vander Stoep, Android Last year, we wrote about why a memory safety strategy that focuses on vulnerability prevention in new code quickly yields durable and compounding gains. This year we look at how this approach isn’t just fixing things, but helping us move faster . The 2025 data continues to validate the approach, with memory safety vulnerabilities falling below 20% of total vul…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Google reports that adopting Rust in Android reduced memory‑safety vulnerability density (2025 data shows memory safety vulnerabilities fell below 20% of total vulnerabilities), reflecting a prevention‑first strategy focused on new code; Rust prevents classes of memory‑safety bugs common in C/C++.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable.\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** Exploit availability unknown.\n- **Patch Available:** Patch availability unknown.\n- **Active Exploitation:** Active exploitation status unknown.\n- **Threat Actors:** None known\n- **Mitigation:** Use memory‑safe languages (Rust) for new code, prioritize vulnerability prevention in code changes, continue auditing C/C++ components and apply defensive coding and sanitizers.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://security.googleblog.com/2025/11/rust-in-android-move-fast-fix-things.html\n\n---\n\n## 8. 🟠 Zero-Day — Mitigating prompt injection attacks with a layered defense strategy\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2025-06-13\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2025/06/mitigating-prompt-injection-attacks.html>\n\n> Posted by Adam Gavish, Google GenAI Security Team With the rapid adoption of generative AI, a new wave of threats is emerging across the industry with the aim of manipulating the AI systems themselves. One such emerging attack vector is indirect prompt injections. Unlike direct prompt injections, where an attacker directly inputs malicious commands into a prompt, indirect prompt injections involve…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Indirect prompt injection (IPI) is an attack where hidden or external instructions (e.g., in emails, documents, calendar invites, or web content) are crafted to manipulate generative AI systems that ingest external data, causing them to disclose sensitive information or perform unauthorized actions. The mechanism relies on models browsing or ingesting untrusted external content which contains adversarial instructions that the model treats as part of its prompt.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable\n- **Exploit Available:** false\n- **Patch Available:** false\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** None known\n- **Mitigation:** Apply a layered defense strategy including input provenance and validation (treat external data as untrusted), content filtering and sanitization, model instruction hardening (instruction‑following constraints and refusal policies), strict data access controls and least‑privilege for model actions, rate‑limiting and monitoring for anomalous queries, and use of browser/browsing isolation when allowing models to access web content.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://security.googleblog.com/2025/06/mitigating-prompt-injection-attacks.html\n\n---\n\n## 9. 🟠 Zero-Day — Countering Chinese State-Sponsored Actors Compromise of Networks Worldwide to Feed Global Espionage System\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** CISA US-CERT Alerts &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** Mon, 25 Au\n**Reference:** <https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-239a>\n\n> Executive summary People’s Republic of China (PRC) state-sponsored cyber threat actors are targeting networks globally, including, but not limited to, telecommunications, government, transportation, lodging, and military infrastructure networks. While these actors focus on large backbone routers of major telecommunications providers, as well as provider edge (PE) and customer edge (CE) routers, th…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Actors modify routers to maintain persistent, long‑term access and leverage compromised devices and trusted connections to pivot into other networks.\n- **Affected Products:** Backbone routers, Provider Edge (PE) routers, Customer Edge (CE) routers\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** Exploit availability unknown.\n- **Patch Available:** Patch availability unknown.\n- **Active Exploitation:** Active exploitation status unknown.\n- **Threat Actors:** Salt Typhoon, OPERATOR PANDA, RedMike, UNC5807, GhostEmperor\n- **Mitigation:** Follow CISA’s mitigation guidance: simulate the threat scenarios, apply router hardening best practices, enforce network segmentation, and regularly update firmware.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-239a\n\n---\n\n## 10. 🟠 Zero-Day — Russian GRU Targeting Western Logistics Entities and Technology Companies\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** CISA US-CERT Alerts &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** Mon, 12 Ma\n**Reference:** <https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-141a>\n\n> Executive Summary This joint cybersecurity advisory (CSA) highlights a Russian state-sponsored cyber campaign targeting Western logistics entities and technology companies. This includes those involved in the coordination, transport, and delivery of foreign assistance to Ukraine. Since 2022, Western logistics entities and IT companies have faced an elevated risk of targeting by the Russian General…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Technical details unavailable\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable\n- **Exploit Available:** Exploit availability unknown\n- **Patch Available:** Patch availability unknown\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** Russian General Staff Main Intelligence Directorate (GRU) 85th Main Special Service Center (85th GTsSS), military unit 26165 (aka APT28)\n- **Mitigation:** Follow advisory hardening and detection recommendations (network segmentation, multifactor authentication, patching where applicable, enhanced monitoring/logging, restrict remote access, incident response planning). See vendor advisory for full mitigations.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-141a\n\n---\n\n## 11. 🟠 Zero-Day — CISA orders feds to patch actively exploited Drupal vulnerability\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Bleeping Computer &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-orders-feds-to-patch-actively-exploited-drupal-vulnerability/>\n\n> CISA has given U.S. government agencies until Wednesday evening to secure their servers against an SQL injection vulnerability in the Drupal content management system (CMS) that it flagged as actively exploited. [...]\n\n---\n\n## 12. 🟠 Zero-Day — KnowledgeDeliver LMS Flaw Exploited to Deploy Godzilla and Cobalt Strike\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2026-5426` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** The Hacker News Security &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/knowledgedeliver-lms-flaw-exploited-to.html>\n\n> A now-patched high-severity security flaw affecting Digital Knowledge KnowledgeDeliver, a Learning Management System (LMS) popular in Japan, was exploited as a zero-day to deliver the Godzilla web shell and ultimately facilitate the deployment of Cobalt Strike Beacon.\n\nThe vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2026-5426 (CVSS score: 7.5), stems from the use of hard-coded ASP.NET machine keys, leading to\n\n---\n\n## 13. 🟠 Zero-Day — [SECURITY ADVISORY] CVE-2026-34474 - ZTE H298A/H108N Unauthenticated Admin Credential Exposure\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2026-34474` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Full Disclosure &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2026/May/20>\n\n> Posted by m.nageh on May 25 -----BEGIN SECURITY ADVISORY----- Advisory ID: MONX-2026-003 CVE ID: CVE-2026-34474 Title: ZTE ZXHN H298A / H108N - Unauthenticated Admin Password &amp; WLAN Credential Exposure Affected: ZTE ZXHN H298A 1.1, ZTE ZXHN H108N 2.6 (EOL; no patch planned) Date: 2026-05-20 Author: Mina Nageh Salalma (Monx Research) Contact: minanageh379 () gmail com Public URL:...\n\n---\n\n## 14. 🟡 High Severity — Microsoft Patches SharePoint RCE Flaw CVE-2026-45659 Across Server Versions\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2026-45659` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** The Hacker News Security &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/microsoft-patches-sharepoint-rce-flaw.html>\n\n> Microsoft has rolled out updates to fix a remote code execution vulnerability impacting SharePoint that could be exploited by bad actors in attacks without requiring any specialized conditions to be met.\n\nThe vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2026-45659, carries a CVSS score of 8.8. It has been assigned an important severity.\n\n&quot;Deserialization of untrusted data in Microsoft Office SharePoint allo…\n\n---\n\n## 15. 🟡 High Severity — Bringing Rust to the Pixel Baseband\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2024-27227` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-04-10\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/bringing-rust-to-pixel-baseband.html>\n\n> Posted by Jiacheng Lu, Software Engineer, Google Pixel Team Google is continuously advancing the security of Pixel devices. We have been focusing on hardening the cellular baseband modem against exploitation. Recognizing the risks associated within the complex modem firmware, Pixel 9 shipped with mitigations against a range of memory-safety vulnerabilities. For Pixel 10, Google is advancing its pr…\n\n---\n\n\n---\n[Live dashboard](https://peleduri.github.io/zero-day-pulse/) · [Raw JSON](https://github.com/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/blob/main/reports/latest.json) · [Action run](https://github.com/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/actions/runs/26454818922)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins/issues/211","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins/issues/211/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins/issues/211/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins/issues/211/events","html_url":"https://github.com/awslabs/agent-plugins/issues/211","id":4796854346,"node_id":"I_kwDORJjPlM8AAAABHeowSg","number":211,"title":"RFC: Vendor Semgrep r/all rules locally with tracked exclusions","user":{"login":"scottschreckengaust","id":345885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NTg4NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/345885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust","html_url":"https://github.com/scottschreckengaust","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10177928750,"node_id":"LA_kwDORJjPlM8AAAACXqbeLg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins/labels/needs-triage","name":"needs-triage","color":"9a06f6","default":false,"description":""},{"id":10177934233,"node_id":"LA_kwDORJjPlM8AAAACXqbzmQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins/labels/RFC-proposal","name":"RFC-proposal","color":"103d75","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"scottschreckengaust","id":345885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NTg4NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/345885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust","html_url":"https://github.com/scottschreckengaust","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-02T17:37:48Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:48:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"scottschreckengaust","id":345885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NTg4NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/345885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust","html_url":"https://github.com/scottschreckengaust","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scottschreckengaust/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":309376,"node_id":"IT_kwDOADJXTM4ABLiA","name":"Feature","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","color":"blue","created_at":"2024-01-25T09:32:58Z","updated_at":"2024-10-08T08:38:53Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nVendor the Semgrep `r/all` community ruleset into the repository so that **all**\nSemgrep invocations (pre-commit, CI, and `mise`) run against a single, pinned,\nlocally-stored ruleset instead of fetching `r/all` live from the registry on\nevery scan. Bake the current rule exclusions into the vendored file, and add a\nhuman-readable document that records the vendored-rules update timestamp plus,\nper decided rule, whether it is active/excluded and why.\n\nThis is a **design + pick-up-and-continue issue**: the design below is complete\nenough for anyone familiar with the project to implement. A task checklist is\nincluded at the bottom.\n\n## Use case\n\nSemgrep runs in three places today, each pointing `--config=r/all` at the live\nSemgrep registry:\n\n- **pre-commit** (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`) — `--config=r/all`, **no** exclude\n  flags (so it currently runs rules the other two paths exclude).\n- **CI** (`.github/workflows/security-scanners.yml`) — `--config=r/all` plus 22\n  `--exclude-rule` flags.\n- **mise** (`mise.toml`, `security:semgrep`) — the same `--config=r/all` plus 22\n  `--exclude-rule` flags on one line.\n\nProblems:\n\n1. **Non-deterministic.** `r/all` evolves upstream; the same commit can scan\n   differently on different days, and new upstream rules appear silently with no\n   review.\n2. **Drift between call sites.** The exclusion list is duplicated by hand, and\n   pre-commit already disagrees with the other two.\n3. **No record of *why* rules are excluded** beyond comments in `.semgrep.yaml`\n   (a stub that Semgrep never actually loads — see verified facts).\n4. **Network dependency.** Every scan fetches rules from the registry.\n\n### Goals\n\n- **(A)** Store the rules locally so any and all `semgrep` calls use them by\n  default, ideally through a standard first-order location rather than per-call\n  flags.\n- **(B)** Maintain a human-readable document recording the vendored-rules update\n  timestamp and, for each decided rule of the `r/all` set, which were excluded\n  and why. Columns: `rule-id`, `rule-description`, `rule-status`\n  (`active` — PR#, `excluded` — PR#, `new`), `rule-updated` (date last changed).\n- **(C)** A mechanism to update (A) and (B).\n\n## Proposal\n\n### Verified facts (empirical, semgrep 1.167.0)\n\nThese drove the design; each was tested directly.\n\n**Configuration lookup order — which rules run:**\n\n| Priority | Source | Behavior |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| 1 | `--config` / `-c` / `-f` CLI flag (repeatable) | Explicit. Accepts a YAML file, a directory of `.yml`/`.yaml`, a URL, or a registry name (`r/all`). |\n| 2 | `SEMGREP_RULES` env var | Used **only when `--config` is absent** (help text: `--config=VAL (absent SEMGREP_RULES env)`). Verified to accept a local **file** and a local **directory**. |\n| 3 | Neither set → `--config auto` | Registry autodetect. With `--metrics=off` it **hard-fails**: `Cannot create auto config when metrics are off`. |\n\nMyth-busters verified:\n\n- **A bare `.semgrep.yaml` in the repo root is NOT auto-loaded.** Dropping it in\n  the working directory with no flag fell through to `auto` and failed. The\n  existing `.semgrep.yaml` (`rules: []`) is a documentation stub Semgrep never\n  reads → it will be removed.\n- **`.semgrepignore` IS auto-loaded** from the project root. It controls *target\n  files*, not *rules*.\n- Loading rules from a **directory** prefixes rule IDs with the directory name\n  (e.g. `rulesdir.no-eval-test`), which would break every `--exclude-rule` ID and\n  every ID in the tracking doc. Loading a **single file** preserves canonical\n  IDs → we vendor a single file.\n\n**Vendoring feasibility:**\n\n- `r/all` downloads as raw YAML from `https://semgrep.dev/c/r/all`:\n  **6.08 MB, 3117 rules**, single file. All 22 currently-excluded IDs are present.\n- Rules carry `metadata.version_id` (opaque, e.g. `LjTz352`), `source`, and\n  `shortlink` — but **no human-readable date**. The `rule-updated` column must be\n  *derived* by diffing `version_id` between snapshots and stamping the date a\n  change is first observed.\n- **Size in git is not the working-tree size.** Raw 6.08 MB → **gzip ~875 KB**\n  (≈ what git stores in a pack and what checkout transfers). A realistic update\n  (version_id bumps + one new rule) added **938 bytes** to the pack after\n  `git gc` — git delta-compresses each snapshot against the prior one, so history\n  growth is negligible. Current repo `.git` is ~2.4 MB. This directly addresses\n  the \"will this slow every checkout\" concern: no, the transferred/stored cost is\n  sub-megabyte and per-update growth is ~1 KB.\n- **Do not strip metadata to save space.** A naive strip of\n  `version_id`/`source`/`shortlink`/`license` lines cut ~20% but silently broke\n  the ruleset (6 findings → 0). Rejected.\n- Co-locating the active file under `tools/semgrep/` does not pollute scan results\n  (Semgrep auto-skips files > 1 MB), but we still add it to `.semgrepignore`\n  explicitly rather than rely on that limit.\n\n### File layout — everything under `tools/semgrep/`\n\n| File | Committed? | Edited by | Role |\n|------|-----------|-----------|------|\n| `r-all.active.yaml` | yes (~875 KB packed) | script only | Pre-filtered rules — excluded rules physically removed. **The only file scans load.** |\n| `rule-state.json` | yes (small) | script only | `rule-id → {version_id, updated}`. Diff baseline + date stamping across runs. |\n| `exclusions.toml` | yes | **humans** | `rule-id → {status, pr, reason}`. Durable source of truth for what is excluded/kept. |\n| `EXCLUSIONS.md` | yes | script only | Generated human-readable tracking table (goal B). |\n| `update.py` | yes | humans | Update mechanism (goal C). |\n| `.tmp/r-all.snapshot.yaml` | **no** | script only | Full verbatim download; transient diff input. Never committed. |\n\nThe full snapshot is not committed because its only job is to be the diff\nbaseline, and `rule-state.json` already holds everything the diff needs\n(`id → version_id`); `update.py` re-downloads it each run anyway. This keeps the\ntracked footprint to a single large file.\n\nThe stub `.semgrep.yaml` is removed (never loaded; misleading).\n\n`.semgrepignore` gains `tools/semgrep/*.yaml` so Semgrep never scans its own rule\nfiles. The gitleaks allowlist/baseline should also exclude\n`tools/semgrep/r-all.active.yaml`, because the vendored ruleset contains\nsecret-detection regexes that would false-positive.\n\n### (A) How scans load the vendored rules\n\nLever: the `SEMGREP_RULES` env var (used whenever `--config` is absent; accepts a\nsingle file). Two layers:\n\n- **`mise.toml` `[env]`:** `SEMGREP_RULES = \"tools/semgrep/r-all.active.yaml\"`.\n  Every bare `semgrep` call in a mise context uses vendored rules with **zero\n  flags** — the \"default via a first-order location\" goal (A) asks for.\n- **pre-commit & CI:** pass `--config tools/semgrep/r-all.active.yaml`\n  **explicitly**, because these run in isolated environments that do not inherit\n  mise's `[env]`. `--config` overrides `SEMGREP_RULES`, so setting both is\n  harmless and consistent.\n\nAll 22 `--exclude-rule` flags are **removed** from `mise.toml` and the CI\nworkflow — exclusions are baked into `r-all.active.yaml`. pre-commit's\n`--config=r/all` (no exclude flags) is replaced by the vendored file, fixing the\nexisting drift. Scans become deterministic (pinned to a snapshot) and work\noffline. `--baseline-commit`/`--baseline`, `--oss-only`, `--metrics=off`, SARIF\noutput, and the CI SARIF post-processing are all unchanged.\n\n### (B) The tracking table — `EXCLUSIONS.md`\n\nHeader records: vendored-snapshot **update timestamp**, Semgrep version, total\nrule count, and counts (active / excluded / new).\n\nTable columns (exactly as specified in goal B):\n\n| rule-id | rule-description | rule-status | rule-updated |\n|---------|-----------------|-------------|--------------|\n| `ai.generic.detect-generic-ai-anthprop.detect-generic-ai-anthprop` | Generic AI provider reference detected | `excluded` — PR#TBD | 2026-06-17 |\n| `ai.generic.detect-generic-ai-oai.detect-generic-ai-oai` | Generic OpenAI reference detected | `excluded` — PR#89 | 2026-06-17 |\n| `elixir.lang.correctness.atom-exhaustion.atom_exhaustion` | Atom exhaustion DoS | `excluded` — PR#TBD | 2026-07-02 |\n| `some.new.rule.appeared` | (newly appeared since last snapshot) | `new` | 2026-07-02 |\n\n- **Scope:** the table lists **decided rules (`active`/`excluded`) plus pending\n  `new` rules** — not all 3117 implicitly-active rules, which would be\n  unreadable. The doc answers \"what did humans decide, and what awaits a\n  decision.\"\n- **`rule-status`:** read from `exclusions.toml`\n  (`excluded — PR#` / `active — PR#`). A rule in the snapshot with no\n  `exclusions.toml` entry renders as `new`.\n- **`rule-description`:** the rule's `message`, first line, truncated.\n- **`rule-updated`:** `update.py` compares each rule's `version_id` against\n  `rule-state.json`; on change (or first sighting) it stamps the run date,\n  otherwise it carries the prior date forward. Derived because `r/all` rules\n  carry no human-readable date.\n\n### (C) The update mechanism — `tools/semgrep/update.py`\n\n`uv run tools/semgrep/update.py`, wired to a `mise run semgrep:update` task, run\nmanually. **No new dependencies** (stdlib `urllib` for download, `tomllib` for\nreading TOML; the script never writes TOML — humans edit it).\n\nFlow:\n\n1. Download `r/all` from `https://semgrep.dev/c/r/all` into `.tmp/`.\n2. Load prior `rule-state.json` (empty on first run).\n3. For each rule: extract `id`, first line of `message`, `version_id`. Mark `new`\n   if no prior entry; bump `updated` to today if `version_id` changed; else carry\n   the prior date forward. Track removed rules.\n4. Load `exclusions.toml`. Build `r-all.active.yaml` = snapshot minus every rule\n   whose `status = excluded`.\n5. Write `r-all.active.yaml`, `rule-state.json`, `EXCLUSIONS.md`.\n6. Print a summary: N new (need triage), N excluded, N changed, N removed.\n\n`update.py` reads the current system date at run time to stamp `rule-updated`;\nbecause it is run manually a normal `date.today()` call is fine. After running,\n`mise run security:semgrep` verifies the active file scans clean.\n\n### Migration (one-time bootstrap)\n\n1. Pre-populate `exclusions.toml` from the 22 existing exclusions — IDs and\n   reasons already documented in `.semgrep.yaml` comments and the CI workflow —\n   with `status = excluded`, the PR# where known (e.g. PR#89 for the OpenAI\n   rule), and `PR#TBD` otherwise.\n2. Run `update.py` once to produce `r-all.active.yaml`, `rule-state.json`, and the\n   first `EXCLUSIONS.md`.\n3. Update the three integration points to point at\n   `tools/semgrep/r-all.active.yaml` and drop the `--exclude-rule` flags.\n4. Add `tools/semgrep/*.yaml` to `.semgrepignore`; add the active file to the\n   gitleaks allowlist/baseline.\n5. Remove the stub `.semgrep.yaml`.\n6. Run `mise run build` to confirm lint, format, and all security scans pass.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- **Scheduled CI auto-update** (a workflow that opens a PR on `r/all` drift).\n  Considered and deferred; updates are manual via `mise run semgrep:update`.\n- **Committing the full snapshot.** `rule-state.json` is the diff baseline.\n- **Metadata stripping / custom minification.** Verified to break rules.\n- **Custom in-house rules.** The layout leaves room for a future\n  `tools/semgrep/custom/` directory, but none are added here.\n\n## Potential challenges\n\n- **Snapshot goes stale.** Mitigated by the visible update timestamp in\n  `EXCLUSIONS.md` and the `new`-rule surfacing that makes drift reviewable.\n- **`r/all` URL/format changes upstream.** `update.py` should fail loudly on a\n  non-YAML or empty download rather than writing a broken active file.\n- **Someone edits `r-all.active.yaml` by hand.** It is script-generated; a header\n  comment in the file and the doc state this. Hand edits are lost on next update.\n- **Isolated environments.** pre-commit/CI do not inherit mise `[env]`, hence the\n  explicit `--config` in those two paths (belt-and-suspenders with the env var).\n\n## Dependencies and Integrations\n\n- **No new tool dependencies.** `update.py` uses Python stdlib only (`urllib`,\n  `tomllib`, `json`); the repo already runs Python tooling via `uv`.\n- **Integrates with** the three existing Semgrep entry points\n  (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`, `.github/workflows/security-scanners.yml`,\n  `mise.toml`), `.semgrepignore`, and the gitleaks baseline/allowlist.\n- **Pins to** Semgrep `1.151.0` (repo's current pinned version) — vendored rules\n  are format-compatible across recent Semgrep releases.\n\n## Alternative solutions\n\n1. **Full file + keep `--exclude-rule` flags.** Simpler diffing but a bare\n   `semgrep` call would still run excluded rules; keeps the drift problem.\n2. **Vendor as a directory of YAMLs.** Rejected — Semgrep prefixes rule IDs with\n   the directory name, breaking every canonical ID used by exclusions and the doc.\n3. **Commit gzipped active file + decompress prestep.** Smallest working tree but\n   adds a decompress step, so \"bare `semgrep` just works\" needs the prestep.\n4. **Don't vendor; keep pulling `r/all` live.** Zero size cost but drops goal (A)\n   (determinism/offline/baked exclusions).\n\n---\n\n## Pick-up-and-continue checklist\n\n- [ ] Create `tools/semgrep/` and `tools/semgrep/update.py` (stdlib only).\n- [ ] Seed `tools/semgrep/exclusions.toml` from the 22 current exclusions\n      (reasons from `.semgrep.yaml` comments + CI; PR# where known, else `TBD`).\n- [ ] Run `update.py` → generate `r-all.active.yaml`, `rule-state.json`,\n      `EXCLUSIONS.md`.\n- [ ] Add `mise run semgrep:update` task in `mise.toml`.\n- [ ] Add `SEMGREP_RULES = \"tools/semgrep/r-all.active.yaml\"` to `mise.toml`\n      `[env]`; remove the 22 `--exclude-rule` flags from `security:semgrep`.\n- [ ] Update `.github/workflows/security-scanners.yml` to\n      `--config tools/semgrep/r-all.active.yaml`; remove the 22 `--exclude-rule`\n      flags (keep baseline/SARIF logic).\n- [ ] Update `.pre-commit-config.yaml` Semgrep hook to\n      `--config=tools/semgrep/r-all.active.yaml` (replacing `--config=r/all`).\n- [ ] Add `tools/semgrep/*.yaml` to `.semgrepignore`; exclude the active file in\n      the gitleaks baseline/allowlist.\n- [ ] Remove the stub `.semgrep.yaml`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run build`; confirm all scanners pass.\n\n<sub>Design captured with assistance from Claude Code.</sub>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins/issues/211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awslabs/agent-plugins/issues/211/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747","id":4037177278,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87wom--","number":747,"title":"[BOUNTY: 50-75 RTC] Bounty Verification Bot — Auto-Verify Star/Follow Claims","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035932,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWuczHA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/major","name":"major","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"50-200 RTC"},{"id":10153071106,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACXSuSAg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/community","name":"community","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Community engagement"},{"id":10356027005,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACaURufQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/development","name":"development","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":202,"created_at":"2026-03-07T03:24:23Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:43:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty Verification Bot\n\nWe spend hours every session manually checking star counts, follow status, wallet existence, and article links. A bot that auto-verifies claims would save massive time.\n\n### What to Build\n\nA GitHub Action or bot that monitors bounty issue comments, detects claims, and posts automated verification results.\n\n### Payout\n\n| Milestone | Reward |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Star/follow verification (reads comment, checks GitHub API, posts result) | **30 RTC** |\n| Wallet existence check (queries RustChain node API) | **+10 RTC** |\n| Article/URL verification (checks dev.to/Medium links are live) | **+10 RTC** |\n| Dev.to article word count + quality check | **+10 RTC** |\n| Duplicate claim detection (checks if user already claimed) | **+15 RTC** |\n\n### How It Should Work\n\n1. **Triggered by**: New comment on bounty issues containing keywords like \"Claiming\", \"Wallet:\", \"Stars:\", \"GitHub:\"\n2. **Checks performed**:\n   - Does user follow @Scottcjn? (`GET /users/{user}/following/Scottcjn` → 204 = yes)\n   - How many Scottcjn repos has user starred? (paginate `/users/{user}/starred`)\n   - Does the claimed wallet exist? (`GET https://50.28.86.131/wallet/balance?miner_id={wallet}`)\n   - Is the claimed article URL live? (HEAD request, check 200)\n   - Has this user already been paid? (check for \"PAID\" in previous comments)\n3. **Posts a verification comment**:\n```\n## Automated Verification for @username\n\n| Check | Result |\n|-------|--------|\n| Follows @Scottcjn | ✅ Yes |\n| Scottcjn repos starred | 45 |\n| Wallet `my-wallet` exists | ✅ Balance: 10.5 RTC |\n| Article link | ✅ Live (dev.to, 612 words) |\n| Previous claims | ⚠️ Paid 25 RTC on #665 |\n\n**Suggested payout**: 45 stars × 1.0 RTC (follows + 45+ multiplier) = 45 RTC\n```\n\n### Technical Requirements\n\n1. **GitHub Action** (preferred) — runs on `issue_comment` webhook\n2. **Secrets needed**: `GITHUB_TOKEN` (for API), `RUSTCHAIN_NODE_URL`\n3. **Rate limit aware** — GitHub API has limits, batch requests efficiently\n4. **No payment execution** — bot ONLY verifies, human approves payment\n5. **Configurable** — bounty rules (rate per star, follow multiplier) in a config file\n6. **Open source** on GitHub\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nManual verification takes 2-5 minutes per claim. With 20+ claims per session, that's over an hour of repetitive API checking. The bot does it in seconds and never makes math errors.\n\nThe human (Scott) still decides whether to pay — the bot just eliminates the grunt work.\n\n### Submit As\n\nStandalone repo with GitHub Action workflow, or PR to a new `Scottcjn/bounty-bot` repo.\n\n**Wallet:** Include your wallet address when claiming.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/755","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/755/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/755/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/755/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/755","id":4037177391,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87wonAv","number":755,"title":"[BOUNTY: 10 RTC] Automated Backup Verification — Validate RustChain DB Backups","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10356027005,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACaURufQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/development","name":"development","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":27,"created_at":"2026-03-07T03:24:28Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:41:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Automated Backup Verification\n\nThe node backs up the SQLite DB, but nobody verifies the backups are valid. A script that tests backup integrity prevents silent data loss.\n\n### Payout\n\n**10 RTC** for a working verification script.\n\n### What to Build\n\nA script that:\n\n1. Finds the latest backup file (`rustchain_v2.db.bak` or similar)\n2. Copies it to a temp location\n3. Runs SQLite integrity check: `PRAGMA integrity_check;`\n4. Verifies key tables exist and have data:\n   - `balances` — has rows with positive amounts\n   - `miner_attest_recent` — has recent attestations\n   - `headers` — has block headers\n   - `ledger` — has transactions\n   - `epoch_rewards` — has reward records\n5. Compares row counts against the live DB (backup shouldn't be more than 1 epoch behind)\n6. Reports PASS/FAIL with details\n7. Optionally alerts on failure (email, webhook, or just exit code)\n\n### Usage\n\n```bash\n# Run as cron job daily\n0 6 * * * /root/rustchain/verify_backup.sh >> /var/log/backup_verify.log 2>&1\n\n# Output:\n# [2026-03-07 06:00:01] Backup: /root/rustchain/backups/rustchain_v2_20260307.db\n# [2026-03-07 06:00:02] Integrity: PASS\n# [2026-03-07 06:00:02] balances: 282 rows (live: 282) ✅\n# [2026-03-07 06:00:02] miner_attest_recent: 18 rows (live: 18) ✅\n# [2026-03-07 06:00:02] headers: 13680 rows (live: 13680) ✅\n# [2026-03-07 06:00:02] RESULT: PASS\n```\n\n### Technical Requirements\n\n1. **Bash or Python** script\n2. **Non-destructive** — never modifies the backup or live DB\n3. **Works on the VPS** — Ubuntu, SQLite3 installed\n4. **Exit code**: 0 = pass, 1 = fail (for cron alerting)\n5. **Handles missing backup gracefully** (reports, doesn't crash)\n\n### Submit As\n\nPR to [Scottcjn/Rustchain](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain) or [Scottcjn/rustchain-monitor](https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-monitor).\n\n**Wallet:** Include your wallet address when claiming.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/755/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/755/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snowdensb/nibrs/issues/481","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snowdensb/nibrs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snowdensb/nibrs/issues/481/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snowdensb/nibrs/issues/481/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snowdensb/nibrs/issues/481/events","html_url":"https://github.com/snowdensb/nibrs/issues/481","id":2279910708,"node_id":"I_kwDOFgNxhs6H5K00","number":481,"title":"moment-2.8.4.min.js: 4 vulnerabilities (highest severity is: 7.5)","user":{"login":"mend-for-github-com[bot]","id":50673670,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NTA2NzM2NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/30796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mend-for-github-com","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mend-for-github-com%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3017567882,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMDE3NTY3ODgy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snowdensb/nibrs/labels/Mend:%20dependency%20security%20vulnerability","name":"Mend: dependency security vulnerability","color":"d1260f","default":false,"description":"Security vulnerability detected by WhiteSource"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-06T02:40:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T00:58:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details><summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/vulnerability_details.png' width=19 height=20> Vulnerable Library - <b>moment-2.8.4.min.js</b></summary>\n\n<p>Parse, validate, manipulate, and display dates</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/moment.js/2.8.4/moment.min.js\">https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mome