user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"fywc","id":124412979,"node_id":"U_kgDOB2pkMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124412979?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc","html_url":"https://github.com/fywc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fywc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"hsliuustc0106","id":222337142,"node_id":"U_kgDODUCYdg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/222337142?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106","html_url":"https://github.com/hsliuustc0106","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"bjf-frz","id":240110042,"node_id":"U_kgDODk_J2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240110042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz","html_url":"https://github.com/bjf-frz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjf-frz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":17,"created_at":"2026-06-11T06:59:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T15:07:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"hsliuustc0106","id":222337142,"node_id":"U_kgDODUCYdg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/222337142?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106","html_url":"https://github.com/hsliuustc0106","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsliuustc0106/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Motivation.\n\n  Cosmos3 covers multiple inference scenarios, including T2I, T2V, I2V, video generation with sound, and action-related generation. These scenarios have different latency, memory, and hardware requirements, especially between Cosmos3-Nano and Cosmos3-Super.\n\n  The goal of this analysis is to provide an evidence-based feature matrix for Cosmos3 across cache acceleration, CPU offload, parallelism, LoRA, quantization, device support, and hardware recipes. It also identifies which features are already supported, which are explicitly unsupported, and which still require validation.\n\n  This document follows the same direction as the continuous diffusion acceleration tracking RFC: maintain a Model x Feature support matrix and clarify Feature x Feature compatibility gaps before recommending production configurations.\n\n### Proposed Change.\n\n#### Features Supported Table\nThe following table tracks Cosmos3 feature support across cache acceleration, offload, parallelism, quantization, LoRA, and execution features. It follows the same status convention as the continuous diffusion acceleration tracking RFC.\n\n | Model | TeaCache | Cache-DiT | UND K/V cache | SP (Ulysses & Ring) | CFG Parallel | Tensor Parallel | Pipeline Parallel | HSDP | CPU Offload (Layerwise) | VAE Patch Parallel | Quantization | LoRA Inference | Step Execution |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Cosmos3-Nano | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |\n  | Cosmos3-Super | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |\n\n#### Quantization\nCosmos3 is marked as quantization-supported at the framework level, and its transformer passes the diffusion `quantization_config` into quantizable linear layers. The current Cosmos3 recipes, however, do not include method-specific validation or recommended quantized checkpoints. Therefore, this section tracks both the framework-level quantization support and the validation status of selected quantization methods.\n  | Model | Quantization Framework | FP8 | NVFP4 |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | Cosmos3-Nano | ✅ | ❓ | ❓ |\n  | Cosmos3-Super | ✅ | ❓ | ❓ |\n\nBeyond the selected FP8 and NVFP4 entries, we welcome contributions for additional GPU and non-GPU quantization methods. On GPUs, potential directions include INT8, ModelOpt-based pre-quantized checkpoints, GGUF-style quantized transformer weights, and other hardware-aware formats supported by the vLLM-Omni quantization framework. On Ascend NPU, the current codebase includes NPU-oriented paths such as INT8, MXFP8, MXFP4, and MXFP4-DualScale, but there is no Cosmos3-specific NPU quantization recipe or validation result yet. Any contribution should clearly document the target device, quantization method, Cosmos3 variant, memory usage, latency, and output quality comparison against the BF16 baseline.\n\n  #### Scenario Optimization\n\n  Cosmos3 supports multiple inference scenarios through the same pipeline, but each scenario has different latency and memory characteristics. This section tracks the baseline configuration and applicable optimization methods for each scenario.\n  | Scenario | Cosmos3-Nano | Cosmos3-Super | Baseline | Optimization | Notes |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Text-to-Image (T2I) | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | `/v1/images/generations`. |\n  | Text-to-Video (T2V) | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | `/v1/videos/sync` without reference image/video. |\n  | Image-to-Video (I2V) | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | `/v1/videos/sync` with image `input_reference` or `image_reference`. |\n  | Video-to-Video (V2V) | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | `/v1/videos/sync` with video `input_reference` or `video_reference`. Use `condition_frame_indexes_vision` and `condition_video_keep`. |\n  | Text-to-Video with Sound (T2VS) | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | T2V plus `generate_sound=true`; output is muxed as MP4 with AAC audio. |\n  | Image-to-Video with Sound (I2VS) | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | I2V plus `generate_sound=true`; output is muxed as MP4 with AAC audio. |\n  | Action Forward Dynamics | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | Input: first frame or video + action trajectory. Output: rollout video. |\n  | Action Policy | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | Input: first frame or video + language instruction. Output: predicted action trajectory + rollout video. |\n  | Inverse Dynamics | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | Input: video. Output: recovered action trajectory. Use async `/v1/videos` to read the top-level `action` field. |\n  | Video-Conditioned Action Generation | ✅ | ✅ |  |  | Input: video under action mode. Output depends on `action_mode`; not generic V2V. |\n\n#### Recipes on varing devices\nThis section tracks documented and missing Cosmos3 deployment recipes across different hardware targets. A recipe should include the target device, model variant, baseline launch command, low-memory optimization flags, and validation results such as memory usage, latency, and output quality. Current documentation covers NVIDIA data-center GPUs, while low-VRAM consumer GPUs and NPU deployments still need validation.\n\n| Device / Hardware | Cosmos3-Nano | Cosmos3-Super | Baseline Recipe | Low-VRAM / Optimization Recipe | Notes |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | 1x NVIDIA H200 / B300 | ✅ | 🙋 | Nano: `vllm serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano --omni --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --init-timeout 1800` | Optional: `--enable-layerwise-offload` for smaller GPUs | Nano has documented 1-GPU online serving recipe. Super requires larger multi-GPU recipe in current docs. |\n  | 2x NVIDIA H200 / B300 | ❓ | ✅ | Super: `vllm serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Super --omni --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --cfg-parallel-size 2 --use-hsdp --hsdp-shard-size 2 --init-timeout 1800` | Optional: `--enable-layerwise-offload` | Documented minimum Super recipe. |\n  | 8x NVIDIA H200 / H100 / A100 | ❓ | ✅ | Super: `vllm serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Super --omni --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --cfg-parallel-size 2 --ulysses-degree 4 --use-hsdp --hsdp-shard-size 8 --init-timeout 1800` | Uses CFG parallel, Ulysses sequence parallel, and HSDP | Documented recommended Super recipe. |\n  | Low-VRAM NVIDIA GPU, e.g. RTX 5090-class | 🙋 | 🙋 |  | Candidate: Nano + `--enable-layerwise-offload`; lower resolution, frame count, and steps; quantization after validation | No documented Cosmos3 recipe or memory result found for this class of GPU. Needs validation. |\n  | Ascend NPU | 🙋 | 🙋 |  | Candidate: NPU quantization paths such as INT8, MXFP8, MXFP4, or MXFP4-DualScale after Cosmos3 validation | No documented Cosmos3 NPU recipe found. |\n  | AMD GPU / ROCm | 🙋 | 🙋 |  | Candidate: ROCm backend validation and ROCm-compatible quantization / attention backend tuning after Cosmos3 validation | No documented Cosmos3 AMD ROCm recipe found. |\n  | Intel XPU, e.g. Intel Arc B-Series | 🙋 | 🙋 |  | Candidate: XPU backend validation, AutoRound / MXFP8 / MXFP4 quantization paths after Cosmos3 validation | No documented Cosmos3 Intel XPU recipe found. |\n\n### Feedback Period.\n\n_No response_\n\n### CC List.\n\n@hsliuustc0106 @Gaohan123 @david6666666 @bjf-frz \n\n### Any Other Things.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Before submitting a new issue...\n\n- [x] Make sure you already searched for relevant issues, and asked the chatbot living at the bottom right corner of the [documentation page](https://vllm-omni.readthedocs.io), which can answer lots of frequently asked questions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm-omni/issues/4340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm-omni/issues/4340/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/smolagents/issues/2117","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/smolagents","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/smolagents/issues/2117/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/smolagents/issues/2117/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/smolagents/issues/2117/events","html_url":"https://github.com/huggingface/smolagents/issues/2117","id":4121672062,"node_id":"I_kwDONZUqgs71q7l-","number":2117,"title":"ENH: Add pre-tool-call authorization layer to MultiStepAgent","user":{"login":"uchibeke","id":5677552,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Nzc1NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5677552?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke","html_url":"https://github.com/uchibeke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uchibeke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7842961978,"node_id":"LA_kwDONZUqgs8AAAAB03oaOg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/smolagents/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-03-23T15:19:17Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:30:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"smolagents has excellent sandboxing (E2B, Modal, Docker, local Python) — but `MultiStepAgent.step()` dispatches tool calls with no authorization layer. Sandboxing prevents system compromise, but doesn't answer: \"was this agent authorized to call this tool?\"\n\nThe Open Agent Protocol (OAP) defines a `before_tool_call` standard (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.18901596) that fits naturally into smolagents' tool dispatch: a `GuardrailProvider` protocol checked before every tool call, with a built-in `AllowlistProvider` for simple cases and the protocol open for custom implementations.\n\nWould you be open to a PR that adds a `guardrail` parameter to `MultiStepAgent` — a `GuardrailProvider` evaluated in `step()` before `tool(**args)` executes? Denied calls would return a structured error observation rather than raising, so the agent can adapt without crashing.\n\nReference implementation https://github.com/bytedance/deer-flow/pull/1240","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/smolagents/issues/2117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/smolagents/issues/2117/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35","id":4819959865,"node_id":"I_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAABH0rAOQ","number":35,"title":"34: Security policy and disclosure docs","user":{"login":"Saber5656","id":177426695,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpNRBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177426695?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656","html_url":"https://github.com/Saber5656","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11434530567,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAACqY0XBw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/labels/v1","name":"v1","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Required for the v1.0.0 release"},{"id":11434531034,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAACqY0Y2g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/labels/wave:5","name":"wave:5","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Verification & release wave"},{"id":11434531242,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAACqY0Zqg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/labels/area:security","name":"area:security","color":"e11d21","default":false,"description":"Security-relevant"},{"id":11434531613,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAACqY0bHQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/labels/area:docs","name":"area:docs","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"Documentation"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-06T14:12:59Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:12:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\n## Summary\n\nPublish the project's security posture: SECURITY.md (reporting, scope,\ncommitments), a public-facing threat-model digest, and a verification\nchecklist that the repo's scanning stack (from issue 02) is actually\narmed.\n\n## Context\n\nDESIGN §9 is the internal model; an OSS release needs the public contract:\nhow to report vulnerabilities, what's supported, what the product promises\n(§9.8) and refuses (ADR-005). GitHub repo settings themselves are\nowner-managed; this issue delivers docs + a verification checklist, not\nsettings changes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `SECURITY.md`, `docs/security-model.md` (public digest)\n- Repo-scanning verification checklist (in the PR description / issue\n  comment, executed with the owner)\n\n## Detailed Requirements\n\n1. `SECURITY.md`:\n   - Reporting: GitHub Security Advisories (private) as the channel; no\n     email required v1; acknowledgment target ≤7 days, fix-or-plan\n     communicated ≤90 days; credit policy.\n   - Supported versions table (latest minor only during v1.x).\n   - **Deployment warnings, verbatim commitments**: never expose\n     `:8443`/`:8080` to the internet (ADR-005 wording); the CA-trust\n     model and what a leaked `data/` implies (CA key!); remote access =\n     your own VPN.\n   - Scope: what counts as a vulnerability here (auth bypass, CSP/CSRF\n     break, token leak, cert mis-issuance, media reaching the hub, DoS\n     below the §9.7 documented floor) vs. not (LAN flooding, physical\n     access to an unlocked station, user removing name constraints).\n   - Signing/checksums status (checksums now; cosign = roadmap).\n2. `docs/security-model.md`: 1–2 page digest of DESIGN §9 for users and\n   reviewers: diagram of trust boundaries (reuse §4 mermaid, simplified),\n   the five §9.8 commitments, residual-risk table (TOFU, user-CA,\n   LAN-DoS) in honest plain language, link to full DESIGN §9. This is the\n   page README's security section links to.\n3. Cross-file consistency: README (32) security summary, SECURITY.md and\n   security-model.md must not drift — single source rule: commitments\n   live word-for-word identical in SECURITY.md and are quoted elsewhere;\n   consistency asserted by a docs-lint grep script (extend\n   `scripts/docs-i18n-check.mjs` sibling `scripts/docs-consistency.mjs`).\n4. Scanning verification checklist (executed with repo owner; results\n   pasted into the issue):\n   `gh api repos/{o}/{r}` + web UI checks — CodeQL runs green on main;\n   Dependabot alerts + security updates enabled; secret scanning + push\n   protection enabled; private vulnerability reporting enabled; branch\n   protection/ruleset on main active. Any gap → owner action item\n   (agent does not change repo settings).\n5. Japanese note: SECURITY.md stays English (GitHub convention);\n   README.ja.md links it with one ja sentence of guidance (coordinate\n   with 33).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] SECURITY.md + security-model.md merged; linked from README and\n      from the admin UI Security panel caption (28 — text-only link\n      addition, coordinate if 28 already merged).\n- [ ] Commitments identical across files (consistency script green;\n      demonstrated failing on a scratch edit).\n- [ ] Private vulnerability reporting verified reachable (test advisory\n      draft created and discarded, or UI screenshot).\n- [ ] Scanning checklist fully executed; each item ✔ or an owner action\n      item filed.\n- [ ] Threat-model digest reviewed against DESIGN §9 for accuracy (no\n      overclaiming — especially around E2E encryption wording: DTLS-SRTP\n      peer-to-peer, hub relays SDP, hub compromise = active-MITM risk,\n      §9.1 wording reused).\n\n## Validation\n\nDocs-consistency script in CI; checklist evidence in the issue; wording\nreview pass.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n01, 02 (scanning stack must exist to verify).\n\n## Non-goals\n\nChanging GitHub org/repo settings (owner-only), bug bounty program, cosign\nsigning implementation (roadmap note only), pentest engagement.\n\n## Design References\n\nDESIGN.md §9 (esp. §9.1, §9.8, §9.10–§9.11); ADR-002, ADR-005;\nISSUE_PLAN §1.\n\n---\n_Derived from [`docs/issues/34-security-policy.md`](https://github.com/Saber5656/openintercom/blob/main/docs/issues/34-security-policy.md) — the repo doc is canonical; update it first if this issue drifts. Design references: [`docs/DESIGN.md`](https://github.com/Saber5656/openintercom/blob/main/docs/DESIGN.md), plan: [`docs/ISSUE_PLAN.md`](https://github.com/Saber5656/openintercom/blob/main/docs/ISSUE_PLAN.md)._\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/magpiecapital/magpie-x402/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/magpiecapital/magpie-x402","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/magpiecapital/magpie-x402/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/magpiecapital/magpie-x402/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/magpiecapital/magpie-x402/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/magpiecapital/magpie-x402/issues/1","id":4624494457,"node_id":"I_kwDOSz6nss8AAAABE6QveQ","number":1,"title":"Build the magpie-x402 MCP server (Lever 1 — distribution multiplier)","user":{"login":"TheMemeBanker","id":253096102,"node_id":"U_kgDODxXwpg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253096102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker","html_url":"https://github.com/TheMemeBanker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMemeBanker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-06-09T18:20:46Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:05:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Highest-leverage distribution work we can ship for agent adoption.**\n\nModel Context Protocol is the de facto standard for AI agents to discover external tools — every major agent runtime supports MCP (Claude Desktop, OpenAI Apps, Cursor, Vercel AI SDK, Continue, Sourcegraph Cody, Replit Agent).\n\nAn MCP server is **one-command-install** for an agent developer. They don't read our README; they don't write x402 payment plumbing; they get tool definitions and call sites for free.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Separate npm package: `@magpiecapital/x402-mcp`\n- Wraps every x402 endpoint in this repo as an MCP tool\n- Auto-handles the x402 payment dance: read endpoints expose as free; paid endpoints accept a `payment_signature` arg and one-shot retry on 402\n- Discover-on-call: pulls `/.well-known/x402.json` once, registers every endpoint listed\n- Includes example MCP server configurations for Claude Desktop, Cursor, and Vercel AI SDK\n\n## Distribution channels (after build)\n\n1. Anthropic MCP marketplace\n2. Glama MCP registry\n3. Smithery MCP registry\n4. Cursor MCP directory\n5. Pinned tweet on @MagpieLoans with the install one-liner\n6. Blog post on magpie.capital: *\"Borrow SOL against your portfolio from inside your Claude conversation\"*\n\n## Why this matters\n\nPer [MARKETING.md](../blob/main/MARKETING.md), this is Lever 1 — the single biggest agent-distribution multiplier we can ship. Everything else (SDK integrations, content, bounties) compounds on top of this.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `@magpiecapital/x402-mcp` published to npm\n- [ ] All currently-shipped endpoints exposed as MCP tools\n- [ ] x402 payment handshake fully abstracted from the agent developer\n- [ ] Submitted to at least the Anthropic + Glama + Smithery registries\n- [ ] README contains a single install + run command for Claude Desktop\n\nSee [MARKETING.md → Lever 1](../blob/main/MARKETING.md#lever-1-mcp-server-distribution-highest-leverage) for the full strategic rationale.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/magpiecapital/magpie-x402/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/magpiecapital/magpie-x402/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}